      <section class="py-5">
        <div class="container custom-webcover">
          <h2 class="text-center mb-3 fw-bold">Evolution of the Web </h2>
          <p class="text-center mb-5 text-justify">Web 3.0 is here, but to understand it better, let's look at where we
            are now and
            how we got here. In just two decades, we've seen enormous developments. Let’s take a peek at the history
            and how the web evolved over time.
          </p>

          <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-3 g-4">
            <div class="col defi-finance-page-styling">
              <div class="card binance-border-card-design defi-finance-page-styling-card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                  <h6 class="card-title mt-2 fw-bold pb-4">Web 1.0 - The Beginning</h6>
                  <p class="card-text text-justify">The first Internet offered what is now known as Web 1.0. Tim
                    Berners-Lee
                    devised the term "Web 1.0" in 1989. Because consumers could only examine the information offered
                    by web pages, this era is often known as the "Read-Only Web." Web 1.0 pages were written in HTML,
                    and the primary communication protocol was HTTP. Websites were developed in the early 1990s using
                    static HTML pages that could only show information. There was no mechanism for users to edit or
                    upload their own data. Simple chat messengers and forums acted as the medium for social
                    interactions.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col defi-finance-page-styling">
              <div class="card binance-border-card-design defi-finance-page-styling-card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                  <h6 class="card-title mt-2 fw-bold pb-4">Web 2.0 - The Read/Write Internet</h6>
                  <p class="card-text text-justify">Darci DiNucci, an author and web designer, coined the term “Web
                    2.0” in 1999
                    to distinguish between the two versions of the web, namely Web 1.0 and Web 2.0. The term was
                    eventually popularized by Tim O'Reilly, the founder of O'Reilly Media. Web 2.0 describes a web in
                    which information flow is two-way. Users could co-author and control the data on the site itself.
                    The most significant contribution of Web 2.0 to humanity was social media sites such as Facebook,
                    Twitter, LinkedIn, and YouTube, among others. These social media sites connected people all over
                    the world in ways that were inconceivable a few decades ago!

                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col defi-finance-page-styling">
              <div class="card binance-border-card-design defi-finance-page-styling-card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                  <h6 class="card-title mt-2 fw-bold">Web 3.0 - The Next Generation Of Internet</h6>
                  <p class="card-text text-justify">In 2014, founder of Polkadot and co-founder of Ethereum, Gavin Wood
                    came up
                    with the term "Web 3.0" to describe his vision for the future of the internet. Web 3 or Web 3.0 is
                    centered on the idea of establishing a completely decentralized environment. This new
                    technological dimension believes in harnessing the power of AI, ML, and cutting-edge technologies
                    such as Blockchain to tackle challenges in today's online platform. In other words, Web 3.0
                    alludes to a completely new and enhanced online environment free of centralized control. It has
                    the ability to take the internet to a whole new level.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

